course: dictionary
lesson: 3775
title: Fondness and liking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «She remembered her grandmother with fondness.» Remembered and grandmother are the clues. Fondness is a gentle, warm liking or love, so the feeling is kind.
explain: Fondness can also mean a liking for doing or eating something. «He has a fondness for cats» tells you what he enjoys, not how he feels about a person. Check the clue words to see which meaning fits.
explain: Strong words can show how much. «An inordinate fondness for beetles» means far more than usual. The words far more than anything else are the clue that the liking is very big.
fact: Fondness is a noun, a word for a feeling or a liking.
fact: «Fondness» means a gentle, warm liking or love for someone or something.
fact: «Fondness» can also mean a liking for doing or eating something, as in «a fondness for chocolate».
fact: Words such as warm, gentle and kind in a sentence are clues that fondness is a soft, happy feeling.
fact: Use the clues around a word, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
exercise: «She remembered her grandmother with fondness.» What does fondness mean here? | *A warm, gentle liking | Hurry and worry | Fear of the dark | Anger at being left out
exercise: «He has a fondness for cats.» What does this tell you about him? | He does not want to be near any animals | *He really likes cats | He has never seen a cat | He is scared of cats
exercise: Find and copy one word from «He has a fondness for cats» that means liking. | has | cats | *fondness | for
test: «Haldane is said to have joked that the creator had an inordinate fondness for beetles.» What does the phrase far more than anything else suggest about fondness here? | A fear of beetles | A wish to sell beetles | *A very strong liking for beetles | A dislike of all insects
test: In «She remembered her grandmother with fondness», which clue shows the feeling is warm? | Fondness is not a feeling | She | *Remembered her grandmother | With
exam: Ella says fondness means being angry with someone. What is the right meaning? | Being bored by something | *A gentle, warm liking | Being angry with someone | Forgetting something you once knew
